  "note": "Tables 3, 5 and 6 to 11 parsed from the PDF text layer (pdfplumber) and then compared value by value against page images rendered at 3x (every table checked, all values agreed). Chart values are the printed data labels from the text layer; each label was assigned to its bar by position (label centred over the bar image, bars grouped into series by drawing order), the series identified from the legend colours on the rendered chart, and each label agreed within 2 points with the bar height measured against the axis ticks; the isolate-weighted chart values also reconcile with the table's overall %R. Page numbers are PDF page numbers (printed page number plus 1)."
 },
 "notes": "First annual report of TARS-Net (state network under NCDC's National Programme on AMR Containment, nodal centre Osmania Medical College, Hyderabad): 13 sites, 16,274 priority-pathogen isolates, 15,674 after removing duplicates. Values are % resistant as printed (intermediate results are not counted as resistant). Genus-level organisms as printed (Klebsiella, Pseudomonas, Acinetobacter and Enterococcus species). Pus aspirate (NCDC definition: aspirated purulent material from a closed infected site; the tables label it PUS) is mapped to deep, the brief's key for aspirates; other sterile body fluids (OSBF) to sterile. Chart rows: IN/EME (inpatients including emergency) mapped to ward. Source inconsistencies kept as printed: E. coli urine and pus rows (see row notes); E. coli Table 8 prints Amoxicillin where the chart prints AMC; Klebsiella Table 9 prints Ampicillin where the chart prints AMC.",
